1
00:01:29,990 --> 00:01:40,790
All right, so while you guys were off doing dumb things like being a rock, getting nosebleeds, or messing with ingredients, I managed to find some patterns in the dungeon's changes.

2
00:01:41,070 --> 00:01:43,490
You make it sound like I wanted to turn to stone!

3
00:01:43,730 --> 00:01:44,810
Yeah, give us a break.

4
00:01:44,950 --> 00:01:46,810
Those three days were very productive.

5
00:01:47,390 --> 00:01:47,890
Uh-huh.

6
00:01:48,910 --> 00:01:51,710
When one place gets blocked, another opens up.

7
00:01:52,010 --> 00:01:53,490
And that happens over and over.

8
00:01:53,930 --> 00:01:57,450
The number of doors, furniture, and building types doesn't change.

9
00:01:57,450 --> 00:02:00,190
The houses won't become cemeteries.

10
00:02:00,730 --> 00:02:03,730
The walls move in a clockwise spiral at set intervals.

11
00:02:04,370 --> 00:02:06,770
And all the statues are in a fixed position.

12
00:02:07,430 --> 00:02:09,550
And then, based on other things.

13
00:02:12,870 --> 00:02:14,710
I recognize this road!

14
00:02:15,150 --> 00:02:17,490
I'm pretty sure that's the house where we ate the dragon.

15
00:02:18,150 --> 00:02:19,510
Chill, Chuck, you're incredible!

16
00:02:20,170 --> 00:02:22,130
Hey, just doing my job.

17
00:02:23,550 --> 00:02:25,450
Hey, wait, isn't this road...

18
00:02:25,450 --> 00:02:27,610
So she remembers it.

19
00:02:27,970 --> 00:02:30,190
We got separated from Fallon here.

20
00:02:30,790 --> 00:02:32,790
Only a trail of blood's been left behind.

21
00:02:33,410 --> 00:02:35,890
If they notice the trail, they'll get worked up.

22
00:02:36,630 --> 00:02:38,110
How am I gonna handle that?

23
00:02:38,450 --> 00:02:39,590
Laios, look there!

24
00:02:40,670 --> 00:02:41,690
Wait a second.

25
00:02:42,170 --> 00:02:42,990
Listen, you guys!

26
00:02:43,190 --> 00:02:47,210
I know there are lots of things to worry about, but for now, we should probably return to the surface?

27
00:02:47,210 --> 00:02:57,050
This was where the dragon's corpse was supposed to be, wasn't it?

28
00:02:57,590 --> 00:03:00,030
Yeah, but it's been cleared away with no remains.

29
00:03:00,590 --> 00:03:02,150
That hole in the wall over there.

30
00:03:02,550 --> 00:03:05,850
Pretty sure it's from when the red dragon fell down after we got the best of it.

31
00:03:06,430 --> 00:03:08,650
It looks almost completely sealed up now.

32
00:03:08,650 --> 00:03:15,010
The eye of the mage is quickly approaching.

33
00:03:17,490 --> 00:03:19,250
Don't just yell all of a sudden!

34
00:03:19,810 --> 00:03:21,230
But I just saw...

35
00:03:21,230 --> 00:03:21,430
Huh?

36
00:03:21,990 --> 00:03:22,430
Uh...

37
00:03:23,810 --> 00:03:24,110
Huh?

38
00:03:24,330 --> 00:03:26,050
Mahana's sickness again, maybe?

39
00:03:26,510 --> 00:03:27,030
Again?

40
00:03:27,490 --> 00:03:31,810
Ever since I used that healing magic, I've been hallucinating and hearing things.

41
00:03:32,310 --> 00:03:33,130
Hearing things?

42
00:03:33,130 --> 00:03:34,910
I'm not sure if that's a symptom.

43
00:03:35,550 --> 00:03:36,570
What was it you heard?

44
00:03:36,890 --> 00:03:39,350
Oh, it said the eye of the mage approaches.

45
00:03:39,850 --> 00:03:41,370
The eye of the mage, huh?

46
00:03:42,550 --> 00:03:44,130
That must mean...

47
00:03:47,070 --> 00:03:49,490
I'm hearing wings.

48
00:03:49,690 --> 00:03:50,710
That small dragon.

49
00:03:50,970 --> 00:03:52,050
We need to go and hide.

50
00:03:52,330 --> 00:03:53,450
Hide where exactly?

51
00:03:53,710 --> 00:03:55,290
Yeah, there's nowhere for us to take cover.

52
00:03:55,870 --> 00:03:56,810
We've gotta run, Marcel.

53
00:03:57,550 --> 00:03:58,230
Not yet.

54
00:03:58,490 --> 00:04:00,130
If we need to hide...

55
00:04:00,790 --> 00:04:02,430
We go in the wall!

56
00:04:03,130 --> 00:04:06,530
Come on!

57
00:04:06,690 --> 00:04:07,670
Hurry up, you two!

58
00:04:08,010 --> 00:04:09,010
What is she?

59
00:04:09,170 --> 00:04:10,830
It's another one of her magic spells?

60
00:04:25,590 --> 00:04:26,910
Tell me, Marcel.

61
00:04:27,310 --> 00:04:29,310
That magic you used...

62
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:30,710
What the hell was that?

63
00:04:30,710 --> 00:04:31,150
Huh?

64
00:04:33,130 --> 00:04:35,810
Wait, cleaners?

65
00:04:36,110 --> 00:04:36,870
Excuse me?

66
00:04:37,550 --> 00:04:38,510
Dungeon cleaners.

67
00:04:38,910 --> 00:04:40,610
They're vital creatures to the dungeon.

68
00:04:40,990 --> 00:04:43,950
Basically, they clean trash and repair places that have been destroyed.

69
00:04:44,530 --> 00:04:44,950
Uh-huh.

70
00:04:45,330 --> 00:04:48,790
The wall wasn't fully restored, so I assumed it hadn't hardened yet.

71
00:04:48,790 --> 00:04:51,470
This part is the original wall.

72
00:04:51,470 --> 00:04:53,550
And the cleaners start down here!

73
00:04:53,950 --> 00:04:54,710
And the floor.

74
00:04:55,010 --> 00:04:58,330
They've even reconstructed it with the wear and tear a normal road would have.

75
00:04:58,970 --> 00:05:00,710
You'd never be able to tell the difference.

76
00:05:02,130 --> 00:05:02,510
Huh?

77
00:05:02,510 --> 00:05:07,490
What the hell are these gross little things crawling all over the ground?

78
00:05:08,290 --> 00:05:08,770
Disgusting.

79
00:05:08,770 --> 00:05:11,150
These are also cleaners.

80
00:05:11,150 --> 00:05:14,470
Any dungeon that didn't have these little guys would fall apart immediately.

81
00:05:14,930 --> 00:05:16,430
And thankfully, they're harmless.

82
00:05:17,390 --> 00:05:18,230
No, they're not.

83
00:05:18,610 --> 00:05:21,770
These pesky little critters are always trying to chew up my tent.

84
00:05:22,830 --> 00:05:25,630
They start destroying whatever they feel is in the way.

85
00:05:25,990 --> 00:05:27,570
Guess that includes your tent, Senshi.

86
00:05:27,570 --> 00:05:31,410
But they're here to eat the dragon's corpse and the rubble from the blast.

87
00:05:32,310 --> 00:05:34,150
They appear when the dungeon receives damage

88
00:05:34,150 --> 00:05:37,410
and use their secretions to stop any further damage.

89
00:05:37,850 --> 00:05:40,470
Then they proceed to eat the debris around the area.

90
00:05:40,970 --> 00:05:41,910
They're not picky.

91
00:05:42,970 --> 00:05:46,290
After that, they use more secretions to cover up holes they find

92
00:05:46,290 --> 00:05:48,710
and restore the dungeon to its original form.

93
00:05:49,550 --> 00:05:51,750
It's the same way living beings heal themselves.

94
00:05:52,190 --> 00:05:53,370
To put it another way,

95
00:05:53,510 --> 00:05:56,170
think of it like how our immune system removes bacteria.

96
00:05:56,170 --> 00:05:57,750
Yeah, I'd rather not.

97
00:05:58,050 --> 00:06:00,530
The way all that works sure feels like some type of magic.

98
00:06:00,670 --> 00:06:01,550
Amazing, right?

99
00:06:02,310 --> 00:06:02,830
Criminy.

100
00:06:03,370 --> 00:06:04,250
What the hell's next?

101
00:06:04,310 --> 00:06:05,850
A magical digestive system?

102
00:06:06,170 --> 00:06:07,410
If that was really a thing,

103
00:06:07,490 --> 00:06:09,050
I wonder what food a dungeon would eat.

104
00:06:11,350 --> 00:06:13,670
I'm glad the blood trail wasn't there anymore.

105
00:06:14,330 --> 00:06:17,730
Hey, let's continue on before another change happens.

106
00:06:26,170 --> 00:06:34,890
It's the stairs! Yay!

107
00:06:36,670 --> 00:06:38,790
Finally, we can get out of this place.

108
00:06:39,290 --> 00:06:39,830
All right.

109
00:06:40,090 --> 00:06:42,470
Now's about the time we should start doing that thing.

110
00:06:42,850 --> 00:06:43,770
Yeah, good point.

111
00:06:44,190 --> 00:06:45,110
Let's do that.

112
00:06:45,490 --> 00:06:46,170
What the...

113
00:06:46,950 --> 00:06:47,810
Oh, right.

114
00:06:47,930 --> 00:06:48,650
Now I get it.

115
00:06:48,650 --> 00:06:58,810
Wait, you guys meant preparing a meal?

116
00:06:59,050 --> 00:07:01,590
I really don't think there are any tentacles on these stairs.

117
00:07:01,750 --> 00:07:02,570
Say that sooner!

118
00:07:03,310 --> 00:07:05,010
You just like wearing that, don't you?

119
00:07:05,070 --> 00:07:05,610
Hell no!

120
00:07:05,610 --> 00:07:10,050
We've got tons of different ingredients.

121
00:07:10,310 --> 00:07:12,270
I'm having a hard time deciding what to make.

122
00:07:13,530 --> 00:07:15,210
Maybe I'll use that new thing.

123
00:07:15,950 --> 00:07:16,690
Cook the barley.

124
00:07:17,170 --> 00:07:19,390
Is that what we picked up from the third floor?

125
00:07:19,690 --> 00:07:22,950
I've been holding on to it in case we ran out of food since it keeps well.

126
00:07:23,870 --> 00:07:25,150
The cockatrice meat,

127
00:07:25,910 --> 00:07:27,050
the dryad fruit,

128
00:07:27,170 --> 00:07:29,190
and the mandrake along with its leaves.

129
00:07:29,910 --> 00:07:31,790
Chop up the depetrification herb.

130
00:07:32,870 --> 00:07:34,570
Season all that and fry it.

131
00:07:35,610 --> 00:07:38,470
Now, stuff some barley rice into the hollowed-out brick.

132
00:07:38,990 --> 00:07:41,530
Top it with the rest and put the brick over the fire.

133
00:07:42,570 --> 00:07:43,930
And then...

134
00:07:43,930 --> 00:07:45,390
What is that thing?

135
00:07:45,710 --> 00:07:47,390
This here's a cockatrice egg.

136
00:07:49,710 --> 00:07:51,750
I'm glad I brought it along with us,

137
00:07:51,910 --> 00:07:54,110
but it's pretty dang difficult to use.

138
00:07:56,670 --> 00:07:58,910
Finally, add the egg sauce over top,

139
00:07:59,010 --> 00:08:00,790
and it's ready.

140
00:08:03,870 --> 00:08:05,470
Whoa, what is this?

141
00:08:05,470 --> 00:08:06,410
This looks tasty.

142
00:08:07,050 --> 00:08:09,090
If I had stayed petrified longer,

143
00:08:09,390 --> 00:08:11,330
would Senshi have used me to make this?

144
00:08:13,850 --> 00:08:18,290
I love this barley rice.

145
00:08:18,770 --> 00:08:20,910
Go on and try stabbing the spoon into the bowl.

146
00:08:20,910 --> 00:08:27,870
I took a couple bricks made by dungeon cleaners and carved them out.

147
00:08:28,510 --> 00:08:30,510
Then does that mean the bowl's edible, too?

148
00:08:31,890 --> 00:08:33,010
This is great.

149
00:08:33,130 --> 00:08:33,890
Thanks, Senshi.

150
00:08:33,890 --> 00:08:34,850
What's it taste like?

151
00:08:34,850 --> 00:08:39,810
What's it taste like?

152
00:08:40,150 --> 00:08:42,070
At first, it just tasted like dirt.

153
00:08:42,670 --> 00:08:44,090
But now that it's settling in,

154
00:08:44,150 --> 00:08:47,290
it's like a magical mixture of cabbage worm, iron, and lemon.

155
00:08:47,650 --> 00:08:49,690
Those are very different things, Laios.

156
00:08:50,230 --> 00:08:52,430
It's pretty hard to describe it properly.

157
00:08:52,430 --> 00:08:55,490
Are you sure it's okay to be eating magical creatures?

158
00:08:55,790 --> 00:08:57,890
You'll hear things and get nosebleeds again.

159
00:08:58,650 --> 00:09:00,290
What are those hallucinations?

160
00:09:00,930 --> 00:09:01,410
Hmm.

161
00:09:02,390 --> 00:09:04,470
When we make it back, you should see a doctor.

162
00:09:04,910 --> 00:09:05,590
Or a shrink.

163
00:09:05,850 --> 00:09:06,290
Why?

164
00:09:06,690 --> 00:09:08,650
Do you think this is some kind of illness?

165
00:09:08,650 --> 00:09:17,390
Wait, is this a hallucination, too?

166
00:09:17,510 --> 00:09:18,930
Can you guys see this thing?

167
00:09:19,630 --> 00:09:21,590
Yeah, I can see it.

168
00:09:22,530 --> 00:09:24,450
Hey, uh, not to interrupt.

169
00:09:25,050 --> 00:09:26,630
But we're under attack here!

170
00:09:31,630 --> 00:09:32,110
Ew.

171
00:09:32,430 --> 00:09:33,370
What are you wearing?

172
00:09:33,950 --> 00:09:35,330
Is it the skin of a frog?

173
00:09:35,330 --> 00:09:38,650
You know, I think the horns on this one's helmet

174
00:09:38,650 --> 00:09:39,810
are just for decoration.

175
00:09:40,850 --> 00:09:41,710
A child, huh?

176
00:09:43,590 --> 00:09:46,250
They could be demons in disguise.

177
00:09:47,310 --> 00:09:49,270
Shall we discover their true nature?

178
00:09:49,930 --> 00:09:51,530
How about we kill one and see if...

179
00:09:51,530 --> 00:09:53,070
Mizaru, that's enough.

180
00:09:54,890 --> 00:09:58,010
I know them.

181
00:09:58,450 --> 00:09:58,930
Shuro!

182
00:10:00,350 --> 00:10:01,790
It's so good to see you!

183
00:10:01,830 --> 00:10:02,610
It's been a while!

184
00:10:02,610 --> 00:10:05,210
I never thought we'd meet in a situation like this!

185
00:10:05,330 --> 00:10:06,650
What a sprawl world!

186
00:10:07,110 --> 00:10:08,150
Did you lose weight?

187
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:17,350
I appreciate it, Shuro.

188
00:10:18,570 --> 00:10:20,610
I'm relieved to see you're doing well, buddy.

189
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:22,350
How overly familiar!

190
00:10:23,030 --> 00:10:23,590
Oh, yeah!

191
00:10:23,790 --> 00:10:24,530
Before I forget.

192
00:10:25,370 --> 00:10:26,930
First up, Senshi.

193
00:10:27,270 --> 00:10:28,070
This is Shuro.

194
00:10:28,230 --> 00:10:29,730
He used to be a member of our party.

195
00:10:30,090 --> 00:10:31,230
Who is this Shuro?

196
00:10:31,230 --> 00:10:32,030
One of the best fighters I've ever seen.

197
00:10:32,030 --> 00:10:33,670
Is he referring to Lord Toshiro?

198
00:10:33,670 --> 00:10:35,710
Not to mention he's about the only person who'd call me a friend.

199
00:10:35,710 --> 00:10:35,890
Toshiro!

200
00:10:38,830 --> 00:10:39,950
That's enough standing.

201
00:10:40,090 --> 00:10:40,870
Come sit with us.

202
00:10:41,530 --> 00:10:42,770
You caught us while we were eating.

203
00:10:43,850 --> 00:10:46,010
You and your friend should...

204
00:10:46,010 --> 00:10:49,370
That's quite the large group you have.

205
00:10:50,690 --> 00:10:52,010
Hey, Kabru.

206
00:10:52,010 --> 00:10:53,350
Kabru, aren't they?

207
00:10:55,790 --> 00:10:56,770
Nice to meet you.

208
00:10:57,950 --> 00:10:59,890
I believe your name is Laios, right?

209
00:11:01,950 --> 00:11:02,350
Yeah.

210
00:11:02,990 --> 00:11:03,770
Nice to meet you.

211
00:11:03,770 --> 00:11:09,370
I wonder just how long it's been.

212
00:11:11,210 --> 00:11:12,210
Hey, Kabru.

213
00:11:12,770 --> 00:11:12,970
Hmm?

214
00:11:13,190 --> 00:11:14,170
It's them, isn't it?

215
00:11:14,390 --> 00:11:15,810
They're the ones who stole our things.

216
00:11:16,490 --> 00:11:17,290
What do we do?

217
00:11:18,050 --> 00:11:18,530
Hmm.

218
00:11:19,450 --> 00:11:20,590
We don't do anything.

219
00:11:20,790 --> 00:11:21,070
Huh?

220
00:11:21,330 --> 00:11:23,430
Then why did we bother coming all this way?

221
00:11:23,430 --> 00:11:23,550
Hmm.

222
00:11:28,150 --> 00:11:29,730
I wanted to meet him in person.

223
00:11:30,550 --> 00:11:30,890
Huh?

224
00:11:30,890 --> 00:11:34,370
I doubt there's any point in asking about the jewels.

225
00:11:35,290 --> 00:11:37,870
There wasn't any guilt on his face when he saw us.

226
00:11:38,710 --> 00:11:41,630
So either he forgot, we blamed the wrong people,

227
00:11:42,030 --> 00:11:44,150
the jewels themselves were a trap from the beginning,

228
00:11:44,770 --> 00:11:45,950
or all of the above.

229
00:11:46,250 --> 00:11:47,670
Did we come here for nothing?

230
00:11:48,190 --> 00:11:49,010
Not at all.

231
00:11:49,530 --> 00:11:50,810
Give me more time to observe.

232
00:11:51,610 --> 00:11:54,030
Aren't you curious about how their party got this far?

233
00:11:54,410 --> 00:11:56,270
Or what they might be planning to do next?

234
00:11:56,730 --> 00:11:57,570
Because I am.

235
00:11:57,570 --> 00:12:02,050
So, I'm assuming you guys have been on this floor for a while now, huh?

236
00:12:02,390 --> 00:12:03,090
That's right.

237
00:12:03,810 --> 00:12:05,970
We've been going in circles trying to get out,

238
00:12:06,210 --> 00:12:07,670
but we keep getting turned around.

239
00:12:08,170 --> 00:12:10,050
We got pretty lost in this place, too.

240
00:12:10,810 --> 00:12:13,530
Lucky for us, Chilchuk discovered a pattern to the changes,

241
00:12:13,850 --> 00:12:15,730
and that's how we managed to make it this far.

242
00:12:16,170 --> 00:12:16,830
That's so.

243
00:12:17,350 --> 00:12:19,470
This is unrelated, but...

244
00:12:19,470 --> 00:12:20,110
Wow, Cheryl.

245
00:12:20,110 --> 00:12:24,550
You're more depraved than I thought.

246
00:12:24,750 --> 00:12:25,970
Are they your other plans?

247
00:12:26,110 --> 00:12:27,210
You've been busy, huh?

248
00:12:28,850 --> 00:12:30,210
They're merely family,

249
00:12:31,010 --> 00:12:32,310
but they're skilled at fighting.

250
00:12:33,910 --> 00:12:35,670
I'm sorry I left the party.

251
00:12:36,670 --> 00:12:39,610
You see, once I realized she wasn't on the surface,

252
00:12:40,290 --> 00:12:42,310
I did what I thought would be the best way

253
00:12:42,310 --> 00:12:43,830
for me to get back into the dungeon,

254
00:12:44,250 --> 00:12:45,950
so I could start searching for her.

255
00:12:45,950 --> 00:12:47,790
My apologies.

256
00:12:48,230 --> 00:12:48,890
It's fine.

257
00:12:49,210 --> 00:12:50,010
We understand.

258
00:12:50,650 --> 00:12:53,870
Although, I'm surprised that you went back in immediately.

259
00:12:54,570 --> 00:12:56,210
Don't you think that was a bit rash?

260
00:12:56,550 --> 00:12:58,110
What if somebody were to get hurt again?

261
00:12:58,350 --> 00:12:59,670
It must have crossed your mind.

262
00:13:01,390 --> 00:13:02,990
Well, for your information,

263
00:13:03,370 --> 00:13:06,850
the four of us were able to defeat the Red Dragon.

264
00:13:08,810 --> 00:13:10,190
Wait, the Red Dragon?

265
00:13:11,250 --> 00:13:13,470
And where... where is...

266
00:13:13,470 --> 00:13:16,850
Cheryl!

267
00:13:17,330 --> 00:13:18,130
My lord!

268
00:13:18,870 --> 00:13:20,130
My lord, I'm begging you,

269
00:13:20,210 --> 00:13:22,050
please eat a meal and get proper sleep.

270
00:13:22,350 --> 00:13:24,570
At this rate, your body will not last long.

271
00:13:24,770 --> 00:13:26,410
You've been pushing yourself that hard?

272
00:13:26,750 --> 00:13:29,630
Elias, anyone with eyes can see that he's not doing well.

273
00:13:30,190 --> 00:13:32,970
Eating a good meal and getting rest is really important.

274
00:13:33,690 --> 00:13:36,670
I have no time for such things.

275
00:13:37,190 --> 00:13:40,550
Cheryl, you shouldn't just eat food when you have the time.

276
00:13:40,550 --> 00:13:43,290
To have the energy to do what you want to do,

277
00:13:43,470 --> 00:13:46,730
you need to eat and sleep when your body tells you that you need it.

278
00:13:48,790 --> 00:13:49,850
Let's eat something.

279
00:13:50,530 --> 00:13:52,750
While we do, I can fill you in on what's happened.

280
00:13:54,910 --> 00:13:55,830
All right, then.

281
00:13:56,690 --> 00:13:59,570
Can you prepare a meal for us, Maizaru?

282
00:13:59,570 --> 00:14:03,790
It's mealtime!

283
00:14:04,190 --> 00:14:05,470
Let us begin preparing!

284
00:14:06,050 --> 00:14:07,950
Tade, you go fetch some water.

285
00:14:08,470 --> 00:14:08,890
Okay.

286
00:14:09,350 --> 00:14:12,630
Hien, Benichidori, you two start preparing the rice.

287
00:14:13,390 --> 00:14:15,290
And Ausebi, your job is...

288
00:14:15,290 --> 00:14:18,690
To protect our lord from harm.

289
00:14:19,090 --> 00:14:21,550
Can't have you adding strange things to the food.

290
00:14:22,010 --> 00:14:24,130
I'll go start lighting a fire for you all.

291
00:14:24,610 --> 00:14:26,090
Oh my, so thoughtful.

292
00:14:26,090 --> 00:14:28,310
I'll leave that to you then, Dwarf.

293
00:14:28,790 --> 00:14:30,210
Food time, yummy, but...

294
00:14:30,210 --> 00:14:32,870
There sure are a lot of people here.

295
00:14:33,750 --> 00:14:36,450
It's not good to have this many people all in one place.

296
00:14:36,970 --> 00:14:38,730
We should split into three groups.

297
00:14:39,450 --> 00:14:39,690
Hmm.

298
00:14:40,390 --> 00:14:41,270
Very well.

299
00:14:42,190 --> 00:14:42,530
Oren!

300
00:14:42,830 --> 00:14:43,110
Huh?

301
00:14:43,350 --> 00:14:43,870
Dwarf!

302
00:14:44,010 --> 00:14:44,250
Huh?

303
00:14:44,630 --> 00:14:45,270
Frog girl!

304
00:14:45,510 --> 00:14:45,810
Frog!

305
00:14:45,810 --> 00:14:49,590
If you're capable of magic, then provide us with a barrier.

306
00:14:50,310 --> 00:14:53,090
It's to prevent monsters from disturbing our lord's meal.

307
00:14:53,090 --> 00:14:57,210
Well, pleasure to meet you, Miss Frog.

308
00:14:57,490 --> 00:14:57,670
Oh.

309
00:14:58,450 --> 00:14:58,970
Same.

310
00:15:00,710 --> 00:15:01,470
All right.

311
00:15:01,670 --> 00:15:02,810
Let's step away from the group.

312
00:15:03,450 --> 00:15:05,030
Ben will tell you everything we've been up to.

313
00:15:05,710 --> 00:15:06,630
Let me help.

314
00:15:07,090 --> 00:15:07,470
Thanks.

315
00:15:08,650 --> 00:15:09,630
Thanks so much, James.

316
00:15:09,630 --> 00:15:10,730
So what I'll tell you.

317
00:15:10,730 --> 00:15:14,090
In this situation, I think the person in the most danger is...

318
00:15:14,630 --> 00:15:16,030
Monsters are yummy.

319
00:15:16,270 --> 00:15:17,410
They're the best!

320
00:15:18,090 --> 00:15:19,710
Monsters cooking food.

321
00:15:19,850 --> 00:15:20,590
Yum, yum.

322
00:15:20,710 --> 00:15:21,490
Eat a lot.

323
00:15:21,490 --> 00:15:23,390
I'll kill you.

324
00:15:24,070 --> 00:15:24,670
Senshi!

325
00:15:25,170 --> 00:15:26,450
I'll come out for the fire!

326
00:15:39,270 --> 00:15:41,910
Hey, aren't you overdoing it a little bit?

327
00:15:42,330 --> 00:15:43,410
So much smoke.

328
00:15:43,410 --> 00:15:47,110
They must have him take a bath after his meal.

329
00:15:47,810 --> 00:15:48,250
Here?

330
00:15:48,750 --> 00:15:50,830
Why don't you have a seat right over there?

331
00:15:51,230 --> 00:15:51,590
Fine.

332
00:15:52,030 --> 00:15:53,510
Now hurry and tell me what's happened.

333
00:15:54,070 --> 00:15:57,370
Well, after you and Namari left the group, the rest of us...

334
00:15:57,370 --> 00:15:58,630
Stick to the main points.

335
00:15:58,630 --> 00:16:03,430
We defeated the Red Dragon, then retrieved Falon and brought her back to life.

336
00:16:03,810 --> 00:16:07,530
But then we were attacked by the Mad Mage, and we got separated.

337
00:16:08,330 --> 00:16:14,570
We decided that we couldn't do this on our own, so we were going back to the surface to ask around for some help.

338
00:16:15,050 --> 00:16:16,230
But we got lost.

339
00:16:16,230 --> 00:16:17,870
You see?

340
00:16:18,390 --> 00:16:20,190
That's why I'm glad we ran into you!

341
00:16:20,490 --> 00:16:21,950
Please, lend us your strength, Shuro!

342
00:16:23,690 --> 00:16:27,190
Mind if I ask a few questions?

343
00:16:28,050 --> 00:16:32,150
The one who created this place is the Mad Mage you mentioned just now, is that correct?

344
00:16:32,950 --> 00:16:37,370
There's only been rumors of his existence, and whoever actually saw him never returned.

345
00:16:38,230 --> 00:16:40,310
How'd you know it was the Mad Mage you saw?

346
00:16:40,310 --> 00:16:44,510
Well, I guess I thought he talked like he fit the part.

347
00:16:44,750 --> 00:16:47,370
And how'd you manage to get away from that dangerous situation?

348
00:16:47,890 --> 00:16:49,130
That was all Marcille.

349
00:16:49,610 --> 00:16:52,850
Oh, she's our magic user, and she held him off.

350
00:16:53,070 --> 00:16:53,870
Can you elaborate?

351
00:16:54,370 --> 00:16:56,390
Well, uh...

352
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:59,330
Magic isn't really my thing, so I couldn't say.

353
00:17:00,450 --> 00:17:01,530
Oh, I see.

354
00:17:03,530 --> 00:17:05,470
May I ask something too, Lyos?

355
00:17:05,470 --> 00:17:05,870
Hmm?

356
00:17:05,870 --> 00:17:15,110
Did I see you eating a brick earlier?

357
00:17:15,830 --> 00:17:15,990
No!

358
00:17:16,370 --> 00:17:17,970
Ah, no, no, no!

359
00:17:18,310 --> 00:17:19,450
It wasn't a brick.

360
00:17:19,610 --> 00:17:22,370
We were eating part of a wall that was made of dungeon cleaners.

361
00:17:22,610 --> 00:17:26,050
We left almost everything behind, including food and money, remember?

362
00:17:26,450 --> 00:17:31,250
So for us to traverse the dungeon faster, we've been eating monsters this entire time!

363
00:17:31,250 --> 00:17:36,970
Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha

364
00:17:39,210 --> 00:17:39,250
That's...

365
00:17:39,350 --> 00:17:39,790
Hmm?

366
00:17:41,530 --> 00:17:43,350
That's actually really interesting.

367
00:17:43,950 --> 00:17:46,590
Well, what's the most delicious thing you've had so far?

368
00:17:46,650 --> 00:17:47,830
Man, I don't know.

369
00:17:47,990 --> 00:17:49,070
That's a hard one.

370
00:17:49,770 --> 00:17:51,030
Kelpie, Living Armour.

371
00:17:51,390 --> 00:17:52,890
You know, it might be the red dragon.

372
00:17:53,150 --> 00:17:53,950
No way!

373
00:17:54,110 --> 00:17:56,050
You ate the red dragon that ate your sister?

374
00:17:56,410 --> 00:17:56,670
Yeah.

375
00:17:57,270 --> 00:17:58,410
You said living armor.

376
00:17:58,710 --> 00:17:59,910
What's even edible on it?

377
00:18:00,090 --> 00:18:01,410
That's an excellent question.

378
00:18:01,810 --> 00:18:04,790
It's actually a mollusk creature that uses the armor as a shell,

379
00:18:04,970 --> 00:18:06,050
just like this sword.

380
00:18:06,590 --> 00:18:06,950
Whoa!

381
00:18:07,210 --> 00:18:08,610
The cleaners are eating Kensuke!

382
00:18:09,050 --> 00:18:10,290
Can't be too careful.

383
00:18:11,130 --> 00:18:13,550
By the way, if you're interested in monster meals,

384
00:18:13,550 --> 00:18:14,830
we can talk about it whenever.

385
00:18:15,550 --> 00:18:17,290
Wow, I appreciate that.

386
00:18:17,650 --> 00:18:18,370
Oh, no.

387
00:18:18,630 --> 00:18:20,710
He's actually serious about this.

388
00:18:21,030 --> 00:18:27,030
Anyway, you had mentioned that you had resurrected Fallon.

389
00:18:27,470 --> 00:18:29,290
Was she safe the last time you saw her?

390
00:18:29,950 --> 00:18:31,090
Uh, yeah.

391
00:18:31,450 --> 00:18:32,650
Do you know where she might be?

392
00:18:33,290 --> 00:18:35,590
There are many places where you can hide on this floor,

393
00:18:35,810 --> 00:18:37,910
but most of them are in orcs' territory.

394
00:18:38,330 --> 00:18:38,790
Oh, yeah.

395
00:18:39,230 --> 00:18:40,430
The orcs shouldn't be an issue.

396
00:18:41,150 --> 00:18:41,410
Oh?

397
00:18:43,790 --> 00:18:44,770
What'd they taste like?

398
00:18:44,810 --> 00:18:45,710
We didn't eat them.

399
00:18:45,810 --> 00:18:46,850
There were some things that happened,

400
00:18:46,930 --> 00:18:48,590
and now we're in a cooperative relationship.

401
00:18:48,590 --> 00:18:49,590
Mm-hmm.

402
00:18:49,590 --> 00:18:51,790
Co-operative relationship?

403
00:18:52,350 --> 00:18:55,430
Technically, it's an adventurous duty to kill any orcs.

404
00:18:56,030 --> 00:18:57,430
Regarding where she is,

405
00:18:57,810 --> 00:19:00,590
it's possible she's on a much deeper floor of the dungeon.

406
00:19:01,390 --> 00:19:03,850
The one who kidnapped her may have taken her there.

407
00:19:04,310 --> 00:19:05,350
Wait, kidnapped?

408
00:19:05,690 --> 00:19:06,450
But why her?

409
00:19:06,730 --> 00:19:08,030
Uh, well...

410
00:19:08,030 --> 00:19:11,350
I think telling Shuro would be fine.

411
00:19:12,350 --> 00:19:14,510
Sorry, but could I talk with him privately?

412
00:19:14,930 --> 00:19:15,370
Sure.

413
00:19:15,570 --> 00:19:16,730
That's not a problem at all.

414
00:19:25,030 --> 00:19:25,550
So?

415
00:19:25,550 --> 00:19:34,230
It's not that field ration pellets are bad,

416
00:19:34,390 --> 00:19:35,630
but having them every day,

417
00:19:36,050 --> 00:19:39,610
I just think you need to have something warm in your belly from time to time.

418
00:19:39,810 --> 00:19:40,550
Cheers to that.

419
00:19:41,010 --> 00:19:43,050
Meals should do a lot more than fill your stomach

420
00:19:43,050 --> 00:19:44,610
until the next chance you get to eat.

421
00:19:44,990 --> 00:19:47,210
You know, you're quite sensible for a dwarf.

422
00:19:47,770 --> 00:19:49,990
Our lord's been sickly ever since childhood.

423
00:19:49,990 --> 00:19:51,870
His appetite was lacking,

424
00:19:52,230 --> 00:19:54,130
and it made everyone around him worry.

425
00:19:55,090 --> 00:19:56,810
However, no matter the situation,

426
00:19:56,990 --> 00:19:59,350
he would always eat the food I prepared for him.

427
00:20:00,170 --> 00:20:02,990
Sometimes I'd be summoned to the kitchen in the middle of an assignment.

428
00:20:03,870 --> 00:20:05,950
He was such an obedient child growing up

429
00:20:05,950 --> 00:20:07,170
that it made me anxious.

430
00:20:08,030 --> 00:20:10,210
The only selfish request he's ever made

431
00:20:10,210 --> 00:20:11,830
was the one that brought us here.

432
00:20:11,830 --> 00:20:13,450
Please, Maizuru.

433
00:20:14,170 --> 00:20:16,010
There's someone that I wish to save.

434
00:20:17,030 --> 00:20:18,010
Lend me your strength.

435
00:20:18,910 --> 00:20:19,330
Oh.

436
00:20:20,870 --> 00:20:23,590
To think some northern girl would steal his heart

437
00:20:23,590 --> 00:20:24,850
during his training journey.

438
00:20:25,390 --> 00:20:27,490
What can I even say to dissuade him?

439
00:20:27,970 --> 00:20:29,770
You really want him to give up?

440
00:20:30,210 --> 00:20:32,090
The head of the family bestowed me

441
00:20:32,090 --> 00:20:34,150
with the task of looking after the young lord,

442
00:20:34,570 --> 00:20:36,650
so I cannot act based on emotion.

443
00:20:37,330 --> 00:20:38,110
In that case,

444
00:20:38,190 --> 00:20:39,890
then what do you think you're doing right now?

445
00:20:39,890 --> 00:20:41,810
If you have preserved foods,

446
00:20:41,910 --> 00:20:43,390
there's no need to go through the trouble

447
00:20:43,390 --> 00:20:44,670
of preparing a fresh meal.

448
00:20:45,610 --> 00:20:45,930
Hmm?

449
00:20:46,710 --> 00:20:48,130
Why do you reckon he ate up

450
00:20:48,130 --> 00:20:49,970
all the things you personally made for him?

451
00:20:50,490 --> 00:20:52,270
Maybe you didn't realize at the time,

452
00:20:52,450 --> 00:20:53,870
but I know what you put in there.

453
00:20:54,110 --> 00:20:57,990
A little ingredient called love.

454
00:21:00,090 --> 00:21:01,390
What are you saying?

455
00:21:01,770 --> 00:21:03,590
Are you proud of yourself for that one?

456
00:21:05,730 --> 00:21:07,470
Although, at this point,

457
00:21:07,470 --> 00:21:08,850
I just might give in.

458
00:21:08,850 --> 00:21:11,510
So, depending on how things turn out,

459
00:21:11,810 --> 00:21:13,950
perhaps I'll put in a good word for those, too.

460
00:21:19,530 --> 00:21:21,530
Why did the art style change so much?

461
00:21:21,770 --> 00:21:23,930
This depiction might be a bit of a stretch,

462
00:21:24,010 --> 00:21:24,570
don't you think?

463
00:21:25,690 --> 00:21:26,130
Yes.

464
00:21:26,550 --> 00:21:27,490
This will suffice.

465
00:21:27,990 --> 00:21:28,890
It's ready!

466
00:21:31,770 --> 00:21:32,550
Hurry, dwarf!

467
00:21:32,550 --> 00:21:34,470
It's important we have my lord eat this

468
00:21:34,470 --> 00:21:35,530
while it's still warm!

469
00:21:36,910 --> 00:21:37,090
Oh?

470
00:21:37,730 --> 00:21:38,450
You two.

471
00:21:38,850 --> 00:21:40,090
Why are you outside?

472
00:21:40,450 --> 00:21:42,310
They said they wanted to speak in private.

473
00:21:43,390 --> 00:21:45,350
My lord, I'm coming in.

474
00:21:46,970 --> 00:21:47,770
My lord!

475
00:21:49,410 --> 00:21:50,710
What is going on?

476
00:21:52,150 --> 00:21:53,550
Did this man do something?

477
00:21:53,550 --> 00:21:56,310
Tell me!

478
00:21:56,510 --> 00:21:57,830
I need to know what happened here!

479
00:21:57,890 --> 00:21:59,890
Sorry, but we couldn't hear from there.

480
00:22:01,430 --> 00:22:02,530
It's black magic.

481
00:22:03,190 --> 00:22:04,310
This man and the others

482
00:22:04,310 --> 00:22:06,170
used black magic and monster flesh

483
00:22:06,170 --> 00:22:07,550
to revive the northern girl.

484
00:22:08,110 --> 00:22:08,550
What?

485
00:22:08,550 --> 00:22:12,630
How could you do such a thing?

486
00:22:13,370 --> 00:22:15,030
Do you even know what you have done?

487
00:22:15,550 --> 00:22:17,390
People who deal with black magic,

488
00:22:17,950 --> 00:22:19,830
the reasons that they have matter not.

489
00:22:20,090 --> 00:22:21,350
They are nothing but criminals!

490
00:22:21,870 --> 00:22:24,430
They get locked in dark cells until they die,

491
00:22:24,730 --> 00:22:26,470
and their corpses are never returned.

492
00:22:26,950 --> 00:22:28,670
If the western elves find out,

493
00:22:28,890 --> 00:22:30,610
then who knows what they'll do to her?

494
00:22:31,270 --> 00:22:33,770
That's assuming this leaves the dungeon, Shuro.

495
00:22:34,570 --> 00:22:36,370
And you won't tell another soul

496
00:22:36,370 --> 00:22:37,490
about any of this happening.

497
00:22:39,010 --> 00:22:39,570
Right?

498
00:22:44,690 --> 00:22:46,530
We had no other options.

499
00:22:47,590 --> 00:22:48,770
Please understand.

500
00:22:51,530 --> 00:22:52,650
Black magic.

501
00:22:53,190 --> 00:22:55,070
This is crazier than I imagined.

502
00:22:55,750 --> 00:22:57,530
How's this gonna turn out?

503
00:23:00,610 --> 00:23:27,310
I must locate you as soon as possible.

